module bankr-ks-local-rules.local-rules

import core.frbp9006.{ frbp9006-kansas }
import frbp.events.{ PetitionFiled }

// The Bankr. D. Kan. court's own periods, counted under FRBP 9006(a). The
// FRBP periods (schedules, claims and the FRBP 3002(c) 70-day bar date,
// exemptions, discharge, the adversary answer, the FRBP 8021 bill of costs
// after appeal and objections to it (LBR 8021.1), new trial and appeals)
// are lit/frbp's and are not declared again; the 30 days of 11 U.S.C. §
// 362(e) and § 362(c)(3) (LBR 4001(a).1, 4001(a).3) and the 7 days before
// the meeting of creditors to give the trustee the last tax return (LBR
// 4002.1(a), § 521(e)(2)(A)) are the Code's, and the governmental bar date
// of LBR 3002.2, the longer of two periods, is noted rather than declared.
// Stated in the rules but not declared: the thresholds after which notices
// may go only to claimants (70 and 90 days, LBR 2002.3) and the 60 days of
// pay advices (LBR 1007.1), which define rather than close; periods counted
// in business days (a protective order motion 4 business days before a Rule
// 2004 examination, LBR 2004.1(c); 3 business days to prove re-insurance of
// a vehicle, LBR 4070.1; 3 business days to report the disposition of a
// preliminary appeal motion, LBR 8010.1); the 48 hours before a deposition
// (LBR 7026.1(d)); the 21 and 28 days' notice of a discharge certification
// or final decree application (LBR 4004.1(a), 3022.1(c)), the 21 days'
// notice of a chapter 7 final distribution (LBR 3001.1(c)) and the 14 days'
// notice that a motion must give before its hearing where no longer notice
// applies, which the movant gives rather than meets, save the filing floor
// of LBR 9013.2(b) declared below; the 35-day disbursement window of LBR
// 3015(b).1(f), the trustee's; the four months in which discovery should be
// completed (LBR 7026.1(b)), hortatory; the 60 days before a motion to show
// cause (LBR 3002.1.1(g)), a floor; the clerk's single 14-day extension of
// time to plead (LBR 5075.1); and Interim LBR 1020.1 (subchapter V
// statements, 14 and 30 days), carried in a standing order outside the
// sectioned rules. The outline's Supreme Court decisions construe the Code
// and the FRBP, not these rules, and are removed here: no reporter text is
// vendored.
/// The arguments and authorities section of a brief or memorandum: not more
/// than 30 pages absent court order (D. Kan. LBR 9013.1(b)).
limit brief-argument { pages <= 30 cite "D. Kan. LBR 9013.1(b)" } cite "D. Kan. LBR 9013.1(b)"

/// The clerk notifies the debtor's attorney, or an unrepresented debtor, of
/// undelivered notices and the matrix deficiency (D. Kan. LBR 2002.1).
event UndeliveredNoticeNotified()
/// The date of a Rule 2004 examination or production (D. Kan. LBR 2004.1).
event ExaminationDate()
/// The chapter 7 trustee mails the summary of the trustee's final report to
/// creditors (D. Kan. LBR 3001.1(c)).
event FinalReportSummaryMailed()
/// A mortgage creditor takes a step to modify the automatic stay in a
/// chapter 12 or 13 case where the secured consumer debt is not paid
/// through the plan (D. Kan. LBR 3002.1.1(d)).
event StayModificationStepTaken()
/// The latest of the order for relief, conversion to subchapter V, or
/// amendment of the petition to designate the case a subchapter V case (D.
/// Kan. LBR 3003.1(a)).
event SubchapterVCaseCommenced()
/// The change of a chapter 13 real property creditor's payee name or
/// payment address (D. Kan. LBR 3015(b).2).
event PayeeChangeDate()
/// The court orders confirmation of a chapter 11 plan (D. Kan. LBR 3022.1,
/// 4004.1(b)).
event ConfirmationOrderEntered()
/// The notice of an alleged default under a chapter 13 Conditional Order
/// Granting Stay Relief is served (D. Kan. LBR 4001(a).1(f)).
event DefaultNoticeServed()
/// A motion to extend or impose the automatic stay under 11 U.S.C. §
/// 362(c)(3) or (c)(4) is served (D. Kan. LBR 4001(a).3(g)).
event StayMotionServed()
/// The debtor files a tax return for the most recent tax year that was
/// unfiled and not yet due at the petition (D. Kan. LBR 4002.1(b)).
event TaxReturnFiled()
/// The trustee requests a copy of an unfiled tax return that was due before
/// the petition (D. Kan. LBR 4002.1(b)).
event TrusteeTaxReturnRequested()
/// The trustee or the United States trustee makes a written request for
/// information to the debtor (D. Kan. LBR 4002.2).
event TrusteeInformationRequested()
/// The meeting of creditors under 11 U.S.C. § 341 concludes (D. Kan. LBR
/// 6007.1).
event MeetingConcluded()
/// A motion to dismiss under FRBP 7012 is served (D. Kan. LBR 7012.1).
event DismissalMotionServed()
/// A response to a motion to dismiss is served (D. Kan. LBR 7012.1).
event DismissalResponseServed()
/// The date of a deposition under FRBP 7030 (D. Kan. LBR 7026.1(c)).
event DepositionDate()
/// A deposition notice is served (D. Kan. LBR 7026.1(d)).
event DepositionNoticeServed()
/// Notice under FRBP 7041 of a motion to dismiss a complaint objecting to
/// discharge is given (D. Kan. LBR 7041.1(b)).
event DischargeDismissalNoticed()
/// The time allowed for appeal of a final order expires, or the clerk
/// receives an order terminating the action on appeal (D. Kan. LBR
/// 7054.1(a)).
event AppealTimeExpired()
/// A motion for summary judgment is served (D. Kan. LBR 7056.1(f)).
event SummaryJudgmentMotionServed()
/// A response to a motion for summary judgment is served (D. Kan. LBR
/// 7056.1(f)).
event SummaryJudgmentResponseServed()
/// An actual hearing is held (D. Kan. LBR 9004.1(c)).
event HearingHeld()
/// The deadline in a notice with objection deadline expires without
/// objection (D. Kan. LBR 9004.1(c)).
event ObjectionDeadlineExpired()
/// The court files an order to show cause why sanctions should not be
/// imposed (D. Kan. LBR 9011.3(a)).
event ShowCauseOrderFiled()
/// The hearing on a motion (D. Kan. LBR 9013.2(b)).
event MotionHearing() paper brief-argument
/// A mediator is initially appointed (D. Kan. LBR 9019.2).
event MediatorAppointed()
/// A notice of removal is filed (D. Kan. LBR 9027.1(b)).
event RemovalNoticeFiled()
/// The court directs an attorney to prepare a journal entry or order, or
/// the parties announce a settlement in court (D. Kan. LBR 9074.1(a)).
event RulingAnnounced()
/// A journal entry or order uploaded without every attorney's approval is
/// served (D. Kan. LBR 9074.1(b)).
event JournalEntryServed()

/// D. Kan. LBR 2002.1: within 7 days after the clerk's notification of
/// undelivered notices, the debtor's attorney, or the debtor if
/// unrepresented, files the corrected BNC Bypass Notice and serves it.
deadline bnc-correction-period: 7.days after UndeliveredNoticeNotified() counted_by frbp9006-kansas cite "D. Kan. LBR 2002.1"
/// D. Kan. LBR 2004.1(b): attendance at a Rule 2004 examination and
/// production of documents may not be required less than 14 days after
/// actual delivery of the notice, except by agreement or court order; a
/// request for production construed under FRBP 7034 is answered in 14 days.
deadline examination-notice-period: 14.days before ExaminationDate() counted_by frbp9006-kansas cite "D. Kan. LBR 2004.1(b)"
/// D. Kan. LBR 3001.1(c): in chapter 7 a priority claim may be filed or
/// amended on or before 14 days after the trustee mails the summary of the
/// final report, or the date final distribution under § 726 commences,
/// whichever is earlier.
deadline priority-claim-amendment-period: 14.days after FinalReportSummaryMailed() counted_by frbp9006-kansas cite "D. Kan. LBR 3001.1(c)"
/// D. Kan. LBR 3002.1.1(d): where the secured consumer debt is not modified
/// or paid through a chapter 12 or 13 plan, the mortgage creditor sends its
/// letter alleging default to the debtor and the debtor's attorney not less
/// than 14 days before taking any step to modify the automatic stay.
deadline mortgage-default-letter-period: 14.days before StayModificationStepTaken() counted_by frbp9006-kansas cite "D. Kan. LBR 3002.1.1(d)"
/// D. Kan. LBR 3003.1(a): in a subchapter V case, unless otherwise ordered,
/// the claims bar date is 70 days after the latest of the order for relief,
/// conversion to subchapter V, or re-designation of the case.
deadline subchapter-v-claims-bar-period: 70.days after SubchapterVCaseCommenced() counted_by frbp9006-kansas cite "D. Kan. LBR 3003.1(a)"
/// D. Kan. LBR 3003.1(a): in a subchapter V case, unless otherwise ordered,
/// the claims bar date for governmental units is 180 days after the latest
/// of the order for relief, conversion to subchapter V, or re-designation
/// of the case.
deadline subchapter-v-governmental-bar-period: 180.days after SubchapterVCaseCommenced() counted_by frbp9006-kansas cite "D. Kan. LBR 3003.1(a)"
/// D. Kan. LBR 3015(b).2: a chapter 13 debtor completes the Mortgage
/// Creditor Checklist and forwards it to the trustee (not the court) within
/// 14 days of the filing of the petition.
deadline mortgage-checklist-period: 14.days after PetitionFiled() counted_by frbp9006-kansas cite "D. Kan. LBR 3015(b).2"
/// D. Kan. LBR 3015(b).2: at least 45 days prior to a change of the real
/// property creditor's payee name or payment address, the creditor notifies
/// the trustee, the debtor and the debtor's attorney by a Notice of
/// Transfer of Servicing and Claim or of Transfer of Claim.
deadline payee-change-notice-period: 45.days before PayeeChangeDate() counted_by frbp9006-kansas cite "D. Kan. LBR 3015(b).2"
/// D. Kan. LBR 3022.1(a): within 3 months after the court orders
/// confirmation of a non-individual chapter 11 plan, the plan proponent
/// files an application for a final decree or shows cause why it cannot be
/// entered; otherwise it files a status report every 6 months until the
/// final decree.
deadline final-decree-application-period: 3.months after ConfirmationOrderEntered() counted_by frbp9006-kansas cite "D. Kan. LBR 3022.1(a)"
/// D. Kan. LBR 4001(a).1(f): if the debtor disputes an alleged default
/// under a Conditional Order Granting Stay Relief, the debtor may file a
/// response within the time the order lists or within 14 days, whichever is
/// later; absent one the movant submits a final order.
deadline conditional-order-default-response-period: 14.days after DefaultNoticeServed() counted_by frbp9006-kansas cite "D. Kan. LBR 4001(a).1(f)"
/// D. Kan. LBR 4001(a).3(b): except for good cause shown in the motion, a
/// motion under 11 U.S.C. § 362(c)(3) is filed within 7 days of the date
/// the petition was filed.
deadline stay-extension-motion-period: 7.days after PetitionFiled() counted_by frbp9006-kansas cite "D. Kan. LBR 4001(a).3(b)"
/// D. Kan. LBR 4001(a).3(g): unless otherwise ordered, an objection to a
/// motion to extend or impose the stay is filed within 14 days after
/// service of the motion.
deadline stay-motion-objection-period: 14.days after StayMotionServed() counted_by frbp9006-kansas cite "D. Kan. LBR 4001(a).3(g)"
/// D. Kan. LBR 4002.1(b): the debtor files the most recent return that was
/// not yet due at the petition when due and provides a signed copy to the
/// trustee within 7 days of its filing.
deadline filed-return-copy-period: 7.days after TaxReturnFiled() counted_by frbp9006-kansas cite "D. Kan. LBR 4002.1(b)"
/// D. Kan. LBR 4002.1(b): the debtor complies with the trustee's request
/// for a copy of a signed, unfiled return due before the petition, the
/// original filed with the taxing authority, within 28 days after the
/// request.
deadline requested-return-period: 28.days after TrusteeTaxReturnRequested() counted_by frbp9006-kansas cite "D. Kan. LBR 4002.1(b)"
/// D. Kan. LBR 4002.2(a): unless the court orders otherwise, a debtor
/// complies with a written request for information by a trustee or the
/// United States trustee within 14 days.
deadline trustee-information-period: 14.days after TrusteeInformationRequested() counted_by frbp9006-kansas cite "D. Kan. LBR 4002.2(a)"
/// D. Kan. LBR 4004.1(b): if a subchapter V plan was confirmed under 11
/// U.S.C. § 1191(a) as a consensual plan, the debtor files a motion for
/// entry of discharge with a simple proposed order within 14 days of entry
/// of the confirmation order.
deadline subchapter-v-discharge-motion-period: 14.days after ConfirmationOrderEntered() counted_by frbp9006-kansas cite "D. Kan. LBR 4004.1(b)"
/// D. Kan. LBR 6007.1(a): within 60 days from the conclusion of the meeting
/// of creditors the chapter 7 trustee may file notice of intended
/// abandonment under § 554 without further service.
deadline abandonment-notice-period: 60.days after MeetingConcluded() counted_by frbp9006-kansas cite "D. Kan. LBR 6007.1(a)"
/// D. Kan. LBR 6007.1(a): unless a creditor or interested party objects
/// within 75 days after the conclusion of the meeting of creditors,
/// property subject to an intended abandonment is deemed abandoned without
/// further notice or order.
deadline abandonment-objection-period: 75.days after MeetingConcluded() counted_by frbp9006-kansas cite "D. Kan. LBR 6007.1(a)"
/// D. Kan. LBR 7012.1(b): a brief or memorandum in response to a motion to
/// dismiss under FRBP 7012 is filed and served within 21 days of service of
/// the motion.
deadline dismissal-response-period: 21.days after DismissalMotionServed() counted_by frbp9006-kansas cite "D. Kan. LBR 7012.1(b)"
/// D. Kan. LBR 7012.1(b): the moving party may file and serve a reply brief
/// within 14 days of service of the response.
deadline dismissal-reply-period: 14.days after DismissalResponseServed() counted_by frbp9006-kansas cite "D. Kan. LBR 7012.1(b)"
/// D. Kan. LBR 7026.1(c): the reasonable notice for taking a deposition
/// under FRBP 7030 is 7 days; for good cause the court may enlarge or
/// shorten it.
deadline deposition-notice-period: 7.days before DepositionDate() counted_by frbp9006-kansas cite "D. Kan. LBR 7026.1(c)"
/// D. Kan. LBR 7026.1(d): a motion for protective order stays a properly
/// noticed deposition only if filed and served within 14 days after service
/// of the deposition notice and at least 48 hours before the deposition.
deadline deposition-protective-motion-period: 14.days after DepositionNoticeServed() counted_by frbp9006-kansas cite "D. Kan. LBR 7026.1(d)"
/// D. Kan. LBR 7041.1(b): if the trustee or the United States trustee
/// objects to dismissal of a complaint objecting to discharge, it moves to
/// intervene and be substituted as plaintiff within 14 days after notice
/// under FRBP 7041.
deadline trustee-intervention-period: 14.days after DischargeDismissalNoticed() counted_by frbp9006-kansas cite "D. Kan. LBR 7041.1(b)"
/// D. Kan. LBR 7054.1(a): a party allowed costs under FRBP 7054(b) files a
/// bill of costs (Form B2630) within 28 days after the time for appeal of a
/// final order expires or the clerk receives an order terminating the
/// action on appeal; failure to file timely waives costs.
deadline bill-of-costs-period: 28.days after AppealTimeExpired() counted_by frbp9006-kansas cite "D. Kan. LBR 7054.1(a)"
/// D. Kan. LBR 7056.1(f): a party has 21 days to file and serve a response
/// to a motion for summary judgment.
deadline summary-judgment-response-period: 21.days after SummaryJudgmentMotionServed() counted_by frbp9006-kansas cite "D. Kan. LBR 7056.1(f)"
/// D. Kan. LBR 7056.1(f): after service of the response, the moving party
/// has 14 days to file and serve a reply memorandum.
deadline summary-judgment-reply-period: 14.days after SummaryJudgmentResponseServed() counted_by frbp9006-kansas cite "D. Kan. LBR 7056.1(f)"
/// D. Kan. LBR 9004.1(c): unless the court directs otherwise, an order
/// resulting from an actual hearing is due 14 days from the date of the
/// hearing.
deadline hearing-order-period: 14.days after HearingHeld() counted_by frbp9006-kansas cite "D. Kan. LBR 9004.1(c)"
/// D. Kan. LBR 9004.1(c): an order resulting from the failure to object or
/// respond to a notice with objection deadline is due 14 days after the
/// deadline expires.
deadline default-order-period: 14.days after ObjectionDeadlineExpired() counted_by frbp9006-kansas cite "D. Kan. LBR 9004.1(c)"
/// D. Kan. LBR 9011.3(a): unless the court orders otherwise, all parties
/// respond within 14 days after the filing of an order to show cause why
/// sanctions should not be imposed.
deadline show-cause-response-period: 14.days after ShowCauseOrderFiled() counted_by frbp9006-kansas cite "D. Kan. LBR 9011.3(a)"
/// D. Kan. LBR 9013.2(b): except for good cause, a motion filed less than
/// 14 days before its hearing may not be considered.
deadline motion-filing-period: 14.days before MotionHearing() counted_by frbp9006-kansas cite "D. Kan. LBR 9013.2(b)"
/// D. Kan. LBR 9019.2: the mediator files a report on the status of the
/// alternative dispute resolution process within 45 days of the initial
/// appointment.
deadline mediator-report-period: 45.days after MediatorAppointed() counted_by frbp9006-kansas cite "D. Kan. LBR 9019.2"
/// D. Kan. LBR 9027.1(b): a motion to remand under FRBP 9027(d) is served
/// within 21 days following the filing of the notice of removal.
deadline remand-motion-period: 21.days after RemovalNoticeFiled() counted_by frbp9006-kansas cite "D. Kan. LBR 9027.1(b)"
/// D. Kan. LBR 9074.1(a): an attorney uploads within 14 days a journal
/// entry or order when the court directs it to prepare one or the parties
/// announce a settlement in court.
deadline journal-entry-period: 14.days after RulingAnnounced() counted_by frbp9006-kansas cite "D. Kan. LBR 9074.1(a)"
/// D. Kan. LBR 9074.1(b): attorneys and unrepresented parties file any
/// objection to entry of a journal entry or order within 14 days after its
/// service; absent a timely objection the court may enter it.
deadline journal-entry-objection-period: 14.days after JournalEntryServed() counted_by frbp9006-kansas cite "D. Kan. LBR 9074.1(b)"

start motion-filed

state motion-filed: "Motion filed and noticed for hearing or with an objection deadline" by applicant cite "D. Kan. LBR 9013.2"
{
  note "A motion is set on the judge's docket with notice of hearing, filed at least 14 days before the hearing, or filed with a separate notice of objection deadline (LBR 9013.2). The motion's FRBP periods are lit/frbp's."
  edge-motion-filed-opposed "Objection filed" -> opposed { authority cite "D. Kan. LBR 9013.2" }
  edge-motion-filed-unopposed "No objection by the deadline" -> ruling {
    authority cite "D. Kan. LBR 9013.2"
  }
}

state opposed: "Objection filed; matter heard" by opponent cite "D. Kan. LBR 9013.2"
{
  note "The notice may provide for hearing on any objection; an order resulting from the hearing is due 14 days after it (LBR 9013.2(c), 9004.1)."
  edge-opposed-ruling "Hearing held" -> ruling { authority cite "D. Kan. LBR 9013.2" }
}

decision ruling: "Motion decided" by court cite "D. Kan. LBR 9013.2"
{
  note "An order on a notice with objection deadline to which no one objected is due 14 days after the deadline expires (LBR 9004.1)."
  edge-ruling-granted "Granted" -> decided { authority cite "D. Kan. LBR 9013.2" }
  edge-ruling-denied "Denied" -> decided { authority cite "D. Kan. LBR 9013.2" }
}

terminal decided: "Matter decided: the case continues under lit/frbp" outcome [procedural] cite "D. Kan. LBR 1001.1"
